NOTE on idealized paths: the prompt header lists an idealized output path
(apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/TripDetailPage.xaml + TripDetailPageViewModel.cs). The real repo is a
C#-markup WinUI 3 app — every sibling W7 page (ChargingDetailPage, DriveDetailPage, TripReplayPage,
BatteryDegradationPage, …) lives under apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Page>/ as
<Page>.{Model,Source,ViewModel}.cs + <Page>.cs (no per-page .xaml; the solution is TeslaSync.sln, not
TeslaSync.App.sln). This unit follows that established convention exactly (verified against ChargingDetailPage /
DriveDetailPage). Pure logic lives in the WinUI-free .Model/.Source/.ViewModel (unit-tested headlessly via the
.csproj <Compile Include> seam); the .cs is the thin view, exercised by the app build.

NOTE on the useTrip contract: the web hook useTrip (web/src/api/hooks/useTrips.ts) is documented @deprecated — the
Go router registers only GET /trips (list), so GET /trips/{id} resolves to a 404 that surfaces through the
PageContainer error path. The port preserves that contract faithfully: TripDetailPageClientFeed issues the single
read and PROPAGATES its failure (it is the primary read) so the view-model folds it into the never-blank error
branch — asserted by Client_feed_propagates_the_primary_read_failure. The generated contract client still pins the
endpoint (ApiEndpoints L500), so the request shaping is real and tested.

NOTE on scope: the manifest enumerates exactly 5 panels (Distance, Energy-Used, Efficiency, Cost, GlassPanel5),
4 states and 12 strings = PARITY_REQUIRED 21. The web page also renders <AIAutoTripNameSuggestion> (an AI
propose-a-name overlay with its own trips.detail.aiSuggestName.* keys). That component is NOT a manifest parity
unit (it is not one of the 5 panels and uses none of the 12 required keys), and wiring an AI-provider feed is
out of scope per "Out of Scope (reject): new product features". It is therefore intentionally not ported; every
one of the 21 manifest items IS implemented. No scope narrowing of the declared 21.

